  "question": {
    "text": "Let the equation of the circle, which touches $x$-axis at the point $(a, 0), a\\gt0$ and cuts off an intercept of length $b$ on $y$-axis be $x^2+y^2-\\alpha x+\\beta y+\\gamma=0$. If the circle lies below $x$-axis, then the ordered pair $\\left(2 a, b^2\\right)$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Vp6l2",
      "text": "$\\left(\\gamma, \\beta^2-4 \\alpha\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vctqg",
      "text": "$\\left(\\alpha, \\beta^2+4 \\gamma\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vcFvT",
      "text": "$\\left(\\gamma, \\beta^2+4 \\alpha\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6tlnZ",
      "text": "$\\left(\\alpha, \\beta^2-4 \\gamma\\right)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e37QcGr6n2VoshC7EVglcReZHrBS7aNYgwjHxnHOh4A.original.fullsize.png\"><br>By pythagoras $\\mathrm{r}^2=\\mathrm{a}^2+\\frac{\\mathrm{b}^2}{4}=\\mathrm{P}^2$\n$r=\\sqrt{\\frac{4 a^2+b^2}{4}}$\n\nEquation of circle is $(x-\\alpha)^2+(y-\\beta)^2=r^2$\n$x^2+y^2-2 a x-2 p y+\\alpha^2+p^2-r^2=0$\ncomparision $x^2+y^2-\\alpha x+\\beta y+r=0$\n$\\begin{array}{r}\n-\\alpha=-2 a, \\beta=-2 p, r=a^2 \\\\\n\\Rightarrow 2 a=\\alpha, 4 a^2+b^2=4 p^2 \\\\\n\\alpha^2+b^2=4 p^2 \\\\\n\\alpha^2+b^2=\\beta^2\n\\end{array}$\n\nSo, $\\left(2 \\mathrm{a}, \\mathrm{b}^2\\right)=\\left(\\alpha, \\beta^2-4 \\mathrm{r}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
